      "gbnf_failure_diagnosis": {
        "observed": "Under GBNF grammar constraint, qwen3-4b emits only whitespace/newlines (grammar ws rule) and never produces the JSON object -> gbnf_success_rate=0.0. Directly reproduced.",
        "root_cause": "qwen3 is a reasoning model that wants a <think> block before any answer. GBNF forbids those tokens, so the constrained sampler is trapped in the only legal filler (ws). Non-reasoning instruct models (gemma3-4b-qat, gemma4-e4b) follow the same grammar at 100%.",
        "implication": "qwen3-4b CANNOT use the production GBNF path for handoffs as-is; it nails prompted-JSON (first-pass 1.0, 0 retries) because <think> is allowed there. UNTESTED hypotheses to recover qwen3+GBNF: (a) prefix-inject empty <think></think> then constrain; (b) disable thinking (/no_think or a non-reasoning qwen variant); (c) grammar permitting a leading think span. VERIFIED conclusion: gemma3/gemma4 are the GBNF-safe workers."
